    "envs": {
      "PYTHONUNBUFFERED": "1",
      "DATA_PATH": "/datasets-storage",
      "MODEL_DIR": "/home/user/project/models"
    },
    "inputs": null,
    "outputs": {
      "accuracy": 0.92
    }
  },
  "valid_json": {
    "name": "image-classification-task",
    "workdir": "/home/user/project",
    "event_callback": "https://example.com/callback",
    "num_nodes": 2,
    "resources": {
      "cpu": "8",
      "memory": "32Gi",
      "gpu": "1"
    },
    "file_mounts": {
      "/datasets-storage": {
        "name": "imagenet-bucket",
        "source": "s3://my-bucket/imagenet",
        "store": "s3",
        "persistent": true,
        "mode": "MOUNT"
      }
    },
    "service": {
      "type": "web",
      "port": 8080,
      "health_check": "/health"
    },
    "setup": "pip install -r requirements.txt",
    "run": "python train.py --epochs 10",
    "envs": {
      "PYTHONUNBUFFERED": "1",
      "DATA_PATH": "/datasets-storage",
      "MODEL_DIR": "/home/user/project/models"
    },
    "inputs": {
      "learning_rate": 0.001
    },
    "outputs": {
      "accuracy": 0.92
    }
  },
  "description": "The image\u2011classification\u2011task will be executed from the project directory\u202f`/home/user/project` on a two\u2011node cluster. Each node is provisioned with eight CPU cores, 32\u202fGiB of memory, and a single GPU. The task mounts the dataset storage at `/datasets-storage` by mounting the S3 bucket named **imagenet\u2011bucket** (source\u202f` s3://my-bucket/imagenet`), with persistence enabled. The environment is prepared with `pip install -r requirements.txt`, and the training is launched via `python train.py --epochs 10`. Key environment variables are set as follows: `PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1`, `DATA_PATH=/datasets-storage`, and `MODEL_DIR=/home/user/project/models`. An input learning rate of\u202f0.001 is supplied, and after the run the expected output metric is an accuracy of\u202f0.92. Upon completion, a callback will be sent to\u202fhttps://example.com/callback.\n\nIn parallel, a lightweight web service is defined for the task, exposing port\u202f8080 and exposing a health\u2011check endpoint at `/health`. The service type is labeled \u201cweb\u201d, allowing external monitoring of the training job while it runs. All configuration details are captured without extra properties, ensuring a clean and reproducible execution environment."
}